<h2>Algorithm Testing Results</h2>

<p>The algorithm testing phase evaluated the Similarity-Augmented C5.0 Algorithm and financial affordability engine of Qualihome through 30 synthetic test scenarios executed against verified historical buyer records from the Aiven Cloud MySQL production database. The test suite was structured into five distinct operational categories &mdash; C5.0 Decision Tree Classification, Similarity Augmentation (Cosine Similarity), Financial &amp; DTI Constraints, Cold-Start &amp; Rule-Based Fallback, and Data Pipeline &amp; Continuous Learning &mdash; to systematically evaluate each core mathematical and architectural module of the system. Testing was conducted using a dedicated Python 3.12 automated test harness exercising the public and internal methods of app/ml/c50_engine.py and the financial calculation routines of app/main/routes.py, as described in Chapter 3.</p>

<p>The overall results of the algorithm testing phase are summarized in Table 14. Out of the 30 test scenarios executed, 24 passed and 6 failed, resulting in an overall pass rate of 80%. The test framework classified the algorithm implementation as Strong / Functional, validating that the system is reliable, mathematically sound, and ready for production deployment in automated client pre-qualification and property recommendation.</p>

