<p>The Cold-Start &amp; Fallback Policy category achieved a perfect pass rate of 100%, verifying that the system safely defaults to deterministic banking rules whenever fewer than 10 training samples exist, successfully capping pseudo-similarity scores to prevent misleading classifications. The Financial &amp; DTI Constraints category achieved an 88% pass rate (7 out of 8 tests passing), demonstrating accurate debt-to-income ratio evaluations, precise Philippine mortgage amortization calculations across multi-year tenures (5, 10, 15, and 20 years), and strict loan ceiling enforcement.</p>

<p>The C5.0 Decision Tree Classification category attained an 86% pass rate (6 out of 7 passing), confirming that entropy-based information gain correctly identifies clear-cut qualified and disqualified applicants. The Similarity Augmentation category achieved an 83% pass rate (5 out of 6 passing), validating that borderline applicant cases (P &lt; 0.72) are reliably augmented by cosine distance against historically approved buyers.</p>

<p>Conversely, the Data Pipeline &amp; Continuous Learning category registered a 40% pass rate, with 3 out of 5 tests failing. The failing tests in this category involved edge-case behaviors during high-concurrency background retrain locking, unhandled foreign currency symbols in raw form submissions, and automated deduplication when sale markers were manually altered.</p>

